ame\": name, \"email\": email})\n}\n\nNeed refactor. External behavior identical: status codes, response bodies. Note original success response: Content-Type set after possible writes? It sets before encode. Body: JSON encoder Encode adds newline. For map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}. Go map iteration order? For two keys, encoding/json sorts keys alphabetically: email then name. So body: {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n. Need preserve. Error bodies no Content-Type set? Original error responses do not set Content-Type. Keep identical. Also no Content-Length? w.Write sets? Not necessarily. We can keep same.\n\nNeed separate functions: parseUserID, fetchUser, writeJSON? But JSON encoding separated. Need clear error handling. Could define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDB? But external behavior identical. Handler maps errors to status/body. Need testable functions.\n\nPotential design:\npackage main\n\nimport (...)\n\nvar db *sql.DB\n\ntype user struct { Name, Email string }\n\nvar (\n errInvalidID = errors.New(\"invalid id\")", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0009350975160486996], [22916, -7.939108371734619]], [[1144, -2.2411597456084564e-05], [513, -11.154281616210938]], [[4087, -0.00950289610773325], [310, -5.07267427444458]], [[1156, -0.02560105174779892], [303, -4.168650150299072]], [[579, -0.32996276021003723], [25, -2.05129337310791]], [[1622, -0.0033798047807067633], [3296, -6.66876220703125]], [[13, -0.44557008147239685], [25, -1.3499757051467896]], [[14235, -0.027343090623617172], [1165, -4.300149440765381]], [[89109, -0.27065378427505493], [7936, -1.942814826965332]], [[5805, -0.00021048614871688187], [2400, -8.986506462097168]], [[9830, -0.026728015393018723], [6795, -3.7003118991851807]], [[6795, -3.349837061250582e-05], [17369, -11.839142799377441]], [[47781, -1.4558922052383423], [1083, -1.5954985618591309]], [[4475, -1.0143204927444458], [2833, -1.07680344581604]], [[2528, -6.246761768124998e-05], [11, -9.717824935913086